```kqml
// Define the sender agent
let agent = {
  label: "sender",
  content: "Analyzing the network scan result for anomalies.",
  language: "KQL"
};

// Create a modal component to display the results
let modal = new Modal();

// Add an input field and labels for the query parameters
modal.addInputField("query", { type: "text" });
modal.addLabel("target", "Target Address");
modal.addLabel("openPorts", "Open Ports");

// Get the scan method from the network scan result
let scanMethod = $(this).find(".scan-method").html();

// Render the modal with the results and update the content of the sender agent
modal.render(agent);
agent.content = scanMethod;
```

This code snippet creates a modal component that displays the output of the network scan result for anomalies. The query parameters include the target address, open ports, and the scan method (e.g., `native-net`), which can be customized based on specific requirements or use cases.

